.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-checks-green 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-checks\-green \- Refuse a head whose required checks are red, still running, or not yet registered
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten checks green\fR [\fB\-\-absent\-ok\fR] [\fB\-\-fanin\fR] [\fB\-J\fR|\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-required\fR> <\fB\-\-answered\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Refuse a head whose required checks are red, still running, or not yet registered
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-required\fR
Comma\-separated check names that carry a verdict about this repository
.TP
\fB\-\-absent\-ok\fR
Comma\-separated check names for which having no run at all is a legitimate reading
.TP
\fB\-\-answered\fR
Comma\-separated conclusions that constitute an answer; anything else is not yet one
.TP
\fB\-\-fanin\fR
The fan\-in check whose failure a cancelled sibling can manufacture
.TP
\fB\-J\fR, \fB\-\-json\fR
Emit byte\-stable JSON instead of pointer lines
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
